sequenceDiagram
    participant S as Sender
    participant N as Network
    participant R as Receiver

    Note over S: outstanding-ack bitmap = 0x00000000
    Note over R: dedup hash[512] empty (mask 0x1FF)

    S->>N: seq 140 reliable
    Note over S: bitmap bit 12 set\nresend timer = 700ms
    N->>R: seq 140 arrives
    Note over R: dedup slot (140 & 0x1FF = 140)\nempty → store + schedule ack

    S->>N: seq 141 reliable
    Note over S: bitmap bit 13 set
    N--xR: seq 141 LOST in transit

    S->>N: seq 142 reliable
    Note over S: bitmap bit 14 set
    N->>R: seq 142 arrives ahead of 141
    Note over R: gap-fill: store at slot 142\nbuffer until 141 fills

    R->>N: ack list = [142, 140]
    N->>S: ack list arrives
    Note over S: processAck clears bits 14 and 12\nbitmap = 0b...0010 (only bit 13 = seq 141)

    Note over S: 700ms elapses for seq 141\nbit 13 still set
    S->>N: seq 141 RETRANSMIT
    Note over S: retransmit_count[141] = 1
    N->>R: seq 141 arrives (late)
    Note over R: dedup slot 141 empty\nstore + ack + deliver 141-142 in order

    R->>N: ack list = [141]
    N->>S: ack arrives
    Note over S: bitmap bit 13 cleared\nbitmap = 0x00000000

    Note over S,R: --- dedup-hit case ---
    S->>N: seq 141 RETRANSMIT (duplicate)
    Note over R: dedup slot 141 already filled\nDROP — ack-only response
    R->>N: ack list = [141]
    N->>S: redundant ack ignored
